  "problem": "The vector $a$ has magnitude $8$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $6$, the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${150}^{\u2218}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n.$  \n\n$a\\times b=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =8\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{150}^{\u2218}\\cdot n \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot n \\\\  & =24n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
